Add `$opening_stores` and selected id after units query. Need handle POST selection. Add:
```
$opening_stores = accessible_stores(null,false);
$opening_warehouse_id = (int)($_POST['opening_warehouse_id'] ?? 0);
if (!$opening_warehouse_id && $opening_stores) ...
```
But top inside POST defines `$opening_warehouse_id` local scoped same function, persists after POST. If GET, undefined. Set after queries:
```
$opening_warehouse_id = (int)($_POST['opening_warehouse_id'] ?? $_SESSION...?)...
```
Use no session. Default first. If POST invalid, selected id remains invalid; but error, render select none selected. Better if invalid fallback first for display. But initial stock error already. `$opening_warehouse_id = find... ? posted : first`. We already computed inside POST. For GET:
```
if (!isset($opening_warehouse_id)) $opening_warehouse_id = (int)($_POST...);
```
Hmm. Simpler after `$units`:
```
$opening_stores = accessible_stores(null,false);
if (!isset($opening_warehouse_id) || !find_accessible_store($opening_warehouse_id,false)) {
   $opening_warehouse_id = $opening_stores ? (int)$opening_stores[0]['warehouse_id'] : 0;
}
```
This makes invalid posting display first, but error shown. Fine.
Add UI.

